.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
implements the parts of an icon-list specific to gevas. 

generic parts are in icon_list. evas-specific parts are in evas2.
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void evas_queue_redraw (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
queue a redraw of the canvas. 
.PP
portability helper so plugins don't need to know about gevas. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "Evas* get_evas_from_iconlist (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
get Evas-pointer from an icon-list. 
.PP
portability helper so plugins don't need to know about gevas. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int gevas_bg_update (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int w, int h)"
.PP
update canvas-background (play along with pseudo-transparency plugins) 
.PP
if present, call \fBbg_upd()\fP in the background plugin to let the plugin know the window was moved/resized, the wallpaper was changed, or whatever. plugins that supply pseudo-transparency may then update the PT pixmap for the given evas icon-list. the plug-in may update the background it whatever manner it sees fit. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP the icon-list 
.br
\fIw\fP the new width 
.br
\fIh\fP the new height
.RE
.PP

.SS "static int gevas_bg_update_x_error (Display * display, XErrorEvent * error)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
catch X error occurring while updating canvas-background (play along with pseudo-transparency plugins) 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIdisplay\fP the display the error is related to 
.br
\fIerror\fP the error
.RE
.PP

.SS "static gboolean gevas_clicked (GtkWidget * widget, GdkEventButton * ev, gpointer data)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
callback: canvas was clicked on 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
TRUE if event was handled conclusively 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIwidget\fP the gevas 
.br
\fIev\fP the click-event 
.br
\fIdata\fP the session
.RE
.PP

.SS "static void gevas_desktop_click (int mx, int my, int mb, int state, unsigned long serial, unsigned long timestamp)\fC [inline, static]\fP"
.PP
forward mouse-click to desktop when evidence handles a desktop, it can forward clicks to the 'original' background (to call up window-manager menus etc. 
.PP
) 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fImx\fP mouse x 
.br
\fImy\fP mouse y 
.br
\fImb\fP mouse buttons (X format) 
.br
\fIstate\fP modifiers (shift etc., X format) 
.br
\fIserial\fP last X event seen 
.br
\fItimestamp\fP when did the event happen?
.RE
.PP

